#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:1
msgid "node-gyp-build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:3
msgid ""
"Build tool and bindings loader for [`node-gyp`][node-gyp] that supports "
"prebuilds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:5
msgid "npm install node-gyp-build\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:9
msgid ""
"[![Test](https://github.com/prebuild/node-gyp-"
"build/actions/workflows/test.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/prebuild"
"/node-gyp-build/actions/workflows/test.yml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:9
msgid "Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:9
msgid ""
".. image:: https://github.com/prebuild/node-gyp-"
"build/actions/workflows/test.yml/badge.svg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:11
msgid ""
"Use together with [`prebuildify`][prebuildify] to easily support "
"prebuilds for your native modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:13
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:15
msgid ""
"**Note.** Prebuild names have changed in [`prebuildify@3`][prebuildify] "
"and `node-gyp-build@4`. Please see the documentation below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:17
msgid ""
"`node-gyp-build` works similar to [`node-gyp build`][node-gyp] except "
"that it will check if a build or prebuild is present before rebuilding "
"your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:19
msgid ""
"It's main intended use is as an npm install script and bindings loader "
"for native modules that bundle prebuilds using "
"[`prebuildify`][prebuildify]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:21
msgid "First add `node-gyp-build` as an install script to your native project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:23
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  \"scripts\": {\n"
"    \"install\": \"node-gyp-build\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:32
msgid ""
"Then in your `index.js`, instead of using the "
"[`bindings`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/bindings) module use `node-"
"gyp-build` to load your binding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:34
msgid "var binding = require('node-gyp-build')(__dirname)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:38
msgid ""
"If you do these two things and bundle prebuilds with "
"[`prebuildify`][prebuildify] your native module will work for most "
"platforms without having to compile on install time AND will work in both"
" node and electron without the need to recompile between usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:41
msgid ""
"Users can override `node-gyp-build` and force compiling by doing `npm "
"install --build-from-source`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:43
msgid ""
"Prebuilds will be attempted loaded from `MODULE_PATH/prebuilds/...` and "
"then next `EXEC_PATH/prebuilds/...` (the latter allowing use with "
"`zeit/pkg`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:45
msgid "Supported prebuild names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:47
msgid ""
"If so desired you can bundle more specific flavors, for example `musl` "
"builds to support Alpine, or targeting a numbered ARM architecture "
"version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:49
msgid ""
"These prebuilds can be bundled in addition to generic prebuilds; `node-"
"gyp-build` will try to find the most specific flavor first. Prebuild "
"filenames are composed of _tags_. The runtime tag takes precedence, as "
"does an `abi` tag over `napi`. For more details on tags, please see "
"[`prebuildify`][prebuildify]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/node-gyp-build-optional-packages/README.md:51
msgid ""
"Values for the `libc` and `armv` tags are auto-detected but can be "
"overridden through the `LIBC` and `ARM_VERSION` environment variables, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

